{
  "case": "lint-draft-integrity-refused",
  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 \u00a76.2 L474 edit runs C -> pre-normalize -> N -> post-normalize under draft; L481 a draft policy does not downgrade integrity, post-N unresolved errors block; \u00a78.2 L631 postcheck; L633 refusal",
  "derivation": "Profile fixture-profile-neutral-lint keeps the vendored validation records. The palette batch of the former create-task-palette-neutral witness (Process_1 holding only Task_1, task-create key k1 value Draft) stages a second unconnected bpmn:Task. C writes nothing; the pre-normalize draft stage evaluates the upstream rules on the C output (bpmnlint 11.15.0 sources: a bpmn:Task without incoming and outgoing sequence flows is reported by no-disconnected, no-implicit-start and no-implicit-end; a Process without StartEvent and EndEvent by start-event-required and end-event-required; label-required and every other recommended rule find nothing; the profile subrule finds no unnamed task). Policy rows: the three connectivity rules error/integrity, the two event rules warn/readiness. An integrity error is never downgraded in draft and is not repairable, so the batch refuses at pre-normalize, before N, with the code of the first unresolved error entry in profile-report/2 order: ruleIds sort end-event-required < no-disconnected < no-implicit-end < no-implicit-start < start-event-required and the Task_1 pointer precedes the new task pointer, so the code is bpmnlint/no-disconnected (harmonization J1, C19). The refusal is atomic: report and diagnostics carry the eight pre-normalize entries (observed, source = the stage element pointer, result unavailable), the tree, IDs and history are unchanged. rawStandardFindings is unsealed (raw upstream transport).",
  "author": "spec-seal",
